<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ămĕthystus</span></b> , i,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέθυστος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The amethyst</i>, <i>a precious stone
				of violet-blue color</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				9, 40, § 121</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Exod.
				28, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Apoc. 21,
			20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of vine</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 2,
				24</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 2, 4, §
		31</span></i>.</div>
